The given equation is \(\sqrt[20]{x^{\log_{2026}x}} = 26x\). Taking the 20th root and rewriting the exponent yields \(x^{\frac{1}{20} \log_{2026} x} = 26x\). Let \(a = \log_{2026} x\), so \(x = 2026^a\). Substituting gives \(2026^{a^2/20} = 26 \cdot 2026^a\). Taking logarithms base 2026 leads to the quadratic equation \(a^2 - 20a - 20 \log_{2026} 26 = 0\). The sum of the roots is \(a_1 + a_2 = 20\), so the product of the corresponding \(x\)-values is \(x_1 x_2 = 2026^{a_1} \cdot 2026^{a_2} = 2026^{20}\).

Factoring \(2026 = 2 \times 1013\), both primes, the product becomes \(2^{20} \times 1013^{20}\). The number of positive divisors is \((20 + 1)(20 + 1) = 441\).

\boxed{441}
